<title>USA: TABLE-Thiokol Q4 June 30 oper shr rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Thiokol Q4 June 30 oper shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>OGDEN, Utah 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>THREE MONTHS ENDED JUNE 30		    Better/</p>
<p>					1997     1996 (Worse)   Percent</p>
<p> Propulsion systems	    $173.8  $164.7    $9.1	   6</p>
<p> Fastening systems		 81.8    63.0    18.8	  30</p>
<p>   TOTAL SALES		    255.6   227.7    27.9	  12</p>
<p>   Net income			23.7    13.3    10.4	  78</p>
<p> Earnings per share		1.26    0.71    0.55	  77</p>
<p> Avg shrs outstanding	    18.8    18.6     0.2	  --</p>
<p>		   (in millions except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: Excluding unusual items in both quarters, fourth quarter net income increased 73 percent or $.52 per share.</p>
<p>12 MONTHS ENDED JUNE 30:			  BETTER/</p>
<p>					1997    1996 (Worse)    Percent</p>
<p>Sales</p>
<p> Propulsion systems	   $606.1  $651.1 $(45.0)	  (7)</p>
<p> Fastening systems	     284.0   238.4    45.6	   19</p>
<p>   Total sales		   890.1   889.5     0.6	   --</p>
<p>   Total Operating income     75.6    61.8    13.8	   22</p>
<p>(Equity income, Howmet)	 30.5     4.5    26.0	  578</p>
<p>   Net income		     82.4    58.3    24.1	   41</p>
<p> Earnings per share	     4.41    3.14    1.27	   40</p>
<p> Avg shrs outstanding	   18.7    18.6     0.1	  --</p>
<p>NOTE: For the year, the company's investment in Howmet Corp contributed $28.3 million to the current year's net income or $1.52 a  share versus the prior year contribution of $4.2 million or $0.23 per share.</p>
<p>Excluding unusual items in both years, fastening systems profit margins increased to 9.2 percent from 5 percent last year.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
